  "support": "A quadrangular marble cinerary urn, without a lid. The rear is plain, the base rough.  Aplain mouling to the top and botoom and the rear edge of teh sides. On the front, relief carving of garlands, horned heads at the upper corners, with a tablet upper centre contianing the inscription; eagles to thelower corners. The left and right sides are carved with acanthus leaves. The inscribed tablet is 19.5 cm wide x 10.8 cm high (and the epigraphic field within it is 16.5 cm wide x 8 cm high)",
